<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benelux</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Benelux Union</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benelux is the union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and Luxembourg. It began as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/customs-union">customs union</a> agreed by their governments in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1944 and in force from 1948, and became an economic union by a treaty of 1958 that took effect in 1960. Its close cooperation served as a model for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-communities">European Communities</a>, which all three countries co-founded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benelux.jpg" alt="Benelux" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hayden120 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Benelux.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
